 "name": "interval-timelapse-insert-awake",
 "description": "Enable interval shooting + time-lapse movie (info 482-486) on the E-PM2 v1.6 by reproducing the E-PL6 1.4 menu wiring exactly: Time Lapse Settings is inserted as global row 11 (Shooting Menu 2, 5th row) and Flash RC Mode moves to row 12 and stays. Alternative to interval-timelapse.json (which replaces Flash RC Mode); see experiments/2026-11-13-intervalometer/README.md section 10. Free space: 0xFF padding 0x7F033C00-0x7F033FFF inside the Usr1 copy 0x80B6A800 -> 0x7ECCB800-0x7F034000 (0x7E504D50: size 0x368800), after the segment-3 constructor table (walked by count, 180 bytes) and one FF word; no code immediate or data word points into 0x7F033B7C-0x7F034000. (a) A 37-row top table (= E-PL6 0x7EFFF864 byte for byte) at 0x7F033C00; the 6 imm32 loads of 0x7EFFE13C (0x7EDEC0A5, 0x7EDEC0FA, 0x7EDEC121, 0x7EDEC7A6, 0x7EDECF42, 0x7EDED085) point to it; the old table stays, unreferenced. (b) .data tab layout (ROM 0x7E8EE8A2, RAM 0x602BE3E2): tab 1 = rows 7-12, later tabs +1, tab-1 count 5 -> 6 (= E-PL6). (c) Page 3's 12-byte child list {13,14,15,16,(628,482),18} (= E-PL6) at 0x7F033D80; the page-3 record pointer 0x7EFFA4B0 points to it. (d) .data per-row value-list pointers (RAM 0x602BE874): Off/On at row 11, rows 11-38 shifted to 12-39. Value switch 0x7EDEC2C0: row constants 13, 31, 32, 33, 34 -> +1 (10 sites); the old row-11 case at 0x7EDEC335 becomes `jmp 0x7F033DE0`, a 51-byte cave that does row 11 -> getSetting(482) and row 12 -> getSetting(180) and returns to the switch (the E-PL6 inserted the same case in line). The 20 `mov 33,d0` row arguments of the formatter 0x7EE01DDA / reverse formatter 0x7EE01E8C in the monitor-adjust panels -> 34 (E-PL6 has 34 at all 20). (e) MODE defaults 483 Frame 0 -> 10, 485 Interval Time 0 -> 5 s. Not ported: the E-PL6 sleep/power-off timer hold (0x7E998F12 calls). NOT BUILT, NOT CAMERA-TESTED. Restore = stock v1.6. KEEP-AWAKE (this file only): the E-PL6's sleep/power-off timer hold during interval shooting is ported with two trampolines in the same padding (0x7F033E20-..., after the insert cave). (f) startIntervalShooting: `jmp 0x7F033E20` at 0x7E98855F (fresh-start branch, after the RTC read, when (32,sp) == 0); the trampoline calls 0x7E997E94 (timer hold, = E-PL6 0x7E998F12) with frame [],4, runs the 6 displaced bytes (clr d0; mov d0,(20,sp); mov sp,a0; add 20,a0) and jumps back to 0x7E988565, as E-PL6 0x7E989552 places the call. (g) The interval sleep-timer selector 0x7E997BD9 becomes `jmp 0x7F033E40`, a rewrite of E-PL6 0x7E998C41 with E-PM2 callees: mode 0, or mode 1 with 482 == 0 or 489 == 487 == 0 -> set interval sleep timer 0x7E997C67(0), then timer restore 0x7E997DC9(0); mode 1 running (489 != 0 or 487 != 0) -> hold 0x7E997E94; mode 2 unchanged (0 or 60001 ms); mode 3 -> 0x7E997C67(0), then hold; other -> the stock assert print. Returns `ret [],16` as the original.",
